				872,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Implement configuration target support and clean up naming\n\nImplement missing ConfigurationTarget handling in UpdateValue.rs:\n- UserLocal now maps to User settings.json (Land has no sync backend)\n- WorkspaceFolder writes to <folder>/.vscode/settings.json for first folder\n- Memory target stores in-memory only (no disk write)\n- Default and Policy targets return read-only errors per spec\n\nAdditionally:\n- Revert binary/lib names from verbose dev identifier back to \"Mountain\"\n- Simplify Tauri identifier to \"land.editor.binary\" and productName to \"Mountain\"\n- Remove duplicate externalBin entry and obsolete .Backup files\n\nThis completes the ConfigurationProvider trait implementation for all VS Code configuration targets, enabling extensions to persist settings to user preferences, workspace .vscode folders, and in-memory session state.",
			"SHA": "1c3dd9e7d4dde40184a53712500b91c447eb2197"
		},
